src/librawspeed/README.md:200:### Canon sRaw/mRaw
src/librawspeed/README.md:201:Canon reduced resolution Raws (mRaw/sRaw) are returned as RGB with 3 component per pixel without whitebalance compensation, so color balance should match ordinary CR2 images. The subsampled color components are linearly interpolated.
src/librawspeed/README.md:203:This is even more complicated by the fact that Canon has changed the way they store the sraw whitebalance values. This means that on newer cameras, you might have to specify "invert_sraw_wb" as a hint to properly decode the whitebalance on these casmeras. To see examples of this, search cameras.xml for "invert_sraw_wb".
